{
  "description": "Bounded prediction data-flow simplification, 2026-11-11. Accept as removal of one staging/conversion layer with preserved movement and no fixed-work CPU regression, not a demonstrated phone speedup.",
  "methodology": "Reuse the existing 1,051-entity recorded crowd client replay: 180 warmup ticks, 600 measured updates and 1200 presentations. Three ordinary trials per lane, before-a / after-a / after-b / before-b / before-c / after-c, followed by separate verify runs. Final timing run starts after this task build/test jobs stop; unrelated OS/background load is not frozen. Earlier overlapping build/test timings are excluded and retained as local logs. Native active-driving fixed schedule separately verifies prediction. One ordinary 10 s clear/jam phone check per lane is a functionality check, with the same v3 work gates and no rematching.",
  "change": {
    "before": "replica ID map -> flat entity array -> repeated finds -> captured request array -> rebuilt private body map -> published copy",
    "after": "borrow existing replica ID map -> owned captured body map -> direct replay handoff -> published copy",
    "removed": "temporary request entity array, its map/filter/map intermediates, repeated whole-array ID searches, and the array/tuple-to-private-map reconstruction. The physics synchronize boundary still takes an array; rendering keeps its ordered array.",
    "preserved": "Independent replica/queued-body/published component ownership, physics body order, missing-metadata holds, input admission, latency and replay scheduling. No pooling, compact schema or clock changes."
  },
